{
  "description": "Authoritative records carry more members than the examples in APIDOCS.md show. WriteRecordAsJson in DnsServerCore/WebServiceZonesApi.cs (v15.5.0) writes name, type, ttl, ttlString, disabled, rData, dnssecStatus, lastUsedOn, lastModified, expiryTtl and expiryTtlString for every record of records/get, records/add and records/update, plus comments when set, nameIdn for internationalized names and glueRecords for NS records with glue addresses. Confirmed with strict response validation of records/get, records/add and records/update against Technitium 15.5.0, 15.5.1 and 15.6.2 containers on 2026-10-31, and for glueRecords against 15.5.0 on 2026-11-01. The rData examples of records/add (an A record) and records/update (an SOA record) each show one record type; both use the rData shape of records/get (see record-data.patch.json), because WriteRecordAsJson writes rData the same way for all three calls.",
